cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "BacLCT: Bacteria Life Cycle Tracking"
message: "If you use this software, please cite the paper below."
type: software
version: 0.4.0
date-released: "2026-08-26"
authors:
  - given-names: Moritz
    family-names: Kunzmann
    email: moritz.kunzmann@bioquant.uni-heidelberg.de
    affiliation: BioQuant, Heidelberg University
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/bmcv/baclct"
abstract: >-
  BacLCT tracks bacteria in time-lapse microscopy and, optionally, classifies their life
  cycle states. Segmented cells become nodes of a temporal graph, a message-passing graph
  neural network classifies each candidate edge as correspondence, division, or no
  correspondence and each node as a life cycle state, and a LAP-based tracker resolves
  them into lineages.
keywords:
  - cell tracking
  - time-lapse microscopy
  - graph neural network
  - bacteria
